## HAND-BACK is mechanical — obey it
`tools/hooks/guard_session.py` → `tools/hooks/guard_assign.py` refuses a dispatch with `HANDBACK REQUIRED (<trigger>)`
when: (a) an unexplained FAIL repeats after its one retry; (b) the same failure class appears twice; (c) a card leaves
the purpose (plan file, memory limit, user rule, goal ids outside the purpose); (d) a user question appears
(decisions_pending grew, or a card is BLOCKED on the user); or a cap is reached (time / USD from the card, runaway
backstop of cards). After that refusal every further dispatch is refused: write the result and end your turn. The
runner re-checks all of it after you exit, so a PURPOSE_MET you write while a trigger stands is overridden.
Hand back yourself, too, whenever continuing would need a decision that is not in the purpose.

